Z||000002||Oreif||07-12-2000||02:30 AM||||I don't remember which thread it was but I thought someone posted that going to a 3.4 DOHC required some cutting near or on the strut tower housing. If I find the thread again I'll let you know which one it is.<P>Found the thread!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/002871.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/002871.html</A> <P>It seems the 3.4DOHC requires a hinge to be trimmed too. see post from Terryk.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 07-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||olympic||07-12-2000||03:27 AM||||  The 3.4 DOHC is the engine the Fiero should hace had all along.  Hi tech and hi revving(7000+ rpm) and very mean sounding.  If you have the chance to purchase a complete engine and 5 speed trans, do it!  The 5 speed is a very rare option.  Its called the Getrag 284.  It has different gears than the Fiero and is stronger.  The engine will bolt up to the Fiero Getrag 282 but I've heard that the gear ratios are not ideal for such a hi revving engine, but I could be wrong here.  The engine also mounts fairly easily to the Fiero cradle.<P>   The kit is $1800 from ACE which includes everything except exhaust.  Most of the work is rewireing everything and some welding.  With the right tools, you probably wouldn't need the kit. <P>------------------<BR>"Born free....taxed to death."||||reg||1
