Z||000018||lowCG||07-13-2000||11:10 PM||||Well,I got everything in order,doesn't want to start however;just pops a little through the exhaust.Might just be old gas,the tank was on empty,and has been sitting for nearly four months.<BR>Terry,what is a good brand of scanner,or does it really matter?<BR>The dogbone has got to go,I'm using Chris West's urethane motor mounts.The coils on my motor were on the passenger's rear of the motor,on top of the timing belt cover.<BR>I'll change to a first gear assignment,thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000019||terryk||07-13-2000||11:53 PM||||I have Diacom, but it is expensive. The Auto X-Ray is fine. About $150 in CA. Make sure it supports your ODB II PCM.<P>What year is your car again? Is it an 88?<P>I forgot that coils were moved on the later engines.<P>Popping... Hmmmm. Assuming you have fuel pressure, the injectors are fired by ignition reference pulses. <P>Any chance your engine has VATS? Vehicle Anti Theft?<P>Terry<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 07-13-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||lowCG||07-14-2000||12:43 AM||||I purchased an anti-theft module that should provide the right signal,the car is an '87.<BR>Something I did,was to switch two of the plugwires on one of the coils(only fit that way),did you say there was a feedback function that would keep me from wanting to do this?<BR>Was going to try some ethyr to see if it could be a fuel supply problem,then on to more expensive things.<BR>After two 12 hour days of sweating in 80 degree Detroit,getting the engine set up into the car,I think I'd better take break.||||reg||1
Z||000021||terryk||07-14-2000||11:34 AM||||Ooooh, 80's. Try 100+ (although we've been lucky in the last week with mid-90's.<P>Assuming the VATS eliminator is working.....<P>The ignition pulses are the trigger for the injectors (in sync mode/normal mode). If you are not getting crank pulses, the injectors won't open. Unless the plug wires are mis-wired, it's hard to get the DIS wired wrong. <BR>And being waste spark, you can swap the wires on any one coil pack and it won't make any difference.<P>It sounds like you have a bad or weak ignition (mis-wired cranks/cam). No ignition pulses will keep the injectors closed and unless one is leaking, there should be no fuel for the popping. Throw a fuel pressure/AC gauge on the rail and see if the pressure drops when you crank it. If so, there are injector pulses. It won't drop much but you will see it move.<P>I've been measuring my 86 and it appears that the dogbone mount can stay unless there is something different about the cam gear covers. That doesn't mean I won't cut that baby out in a second. I hope to get it into the car in the next two weeks.<P>Terry<P><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000022||lowCG||07-14-2000||11:39 AM||||Waahhoo!<BR>The $2.29 can of ethyr has started the car,along with a gallon of Sunoco's finest.<BR>Probably a good idea to have a scanner though.I'll road test the car,and if I get the fuel/spark delay,I'll try the gear assignment to first gear.<BR>Think I'll wait for my underdrive pulley to arrive before any more testing.<BR>Terry,do these systems allow a 2000rpm idle when cold? Was wondering if I'm really running in a disabled mode possibly.||||reg||1
Z||000023||Dan86gt3.8||07-14-2000||12:25 PM||||Glad to see you guys swapping.  How do you think the 3.4 will pull in the higher rpm's?  is there a feul cut off at 7k?  My mom has a monte carlo z34 with the tdc and her tach is redlined at 7k.  But her auto shifts before it gets close to the 7k mark.  And I did not try to leave it in gear as it is my moms car not mine and I would be in a world of ****  if I blew it up.  Are both you guys using manual tranny's?  and did both of you do the wiring harness yourself??  Also lowcg, do chris wests mounts bolt right up to the engine then bolt right in the cradle or do you have to drill or weld the cradle?  Anyways keep up the good work.  And lowcg are you going to the track after you get everything running right?  Hopefully I will have a time by the 21st (we are going to ennis on friday night).  Ohhand to whoever though 80's was hot come down to texas and you will not see it below 80 till september!  You should be thanking the god of good weather that its 80!!!!!<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>15" konig monsoon's<BR>rear swaybar/ and urethane on rear.<BR>Soon to come urethane all the way around. and new yellow paint w/ raised spoiler!!!!<BR>(also in way future years forced induction on my 3.8!!!!!!!!!)||||reg||1
Z||000024||terryk||07-14-2000||01:34 PM||||LowCG,<P>Please keep me posted on what you find. I'm trying to catch up!!!!<P>Dan86gt3.8,<P>I'm doing my own wiring. It's all labor. I wouldn't dream of paying someone for a harness. <P>For my 86 car, I just had to grind two grooves in the crank-side L-bracket so it would clear two ribs on the back of the timing belt/accessories cover. It bolted to the block in the normal location. That was the only change. No cradle or Getrag mount changes. Otherwise stock 86 V6 motor mounts.<P>I don't know where the revlimiter is set on the 96 and up engines. I have a Diacom run of 96 engine running the 92/93 ECM/code winding to 7850 RPM. Sounded fine. In fact it almost sounded *Indy*.<P>We made some, er, *changes* to the code to ignore the limiter. I let him try it first.<BR>It worked. <P>Frankly, I wouldn't go much above 7000, but hey, it did it fine.<P>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000025||lowCG||07-14-2000||05:27 PM||||I've always liked the higher winding motors,7800 sounds great I'll bet!<BR>Chris West's motor mounts bolted in without any drilling,eliminated any need to fabricate a dogbone,but I'll measure around for you Terry and tell you how much room is available.I still need to get the rubber boot that connects the air cleaner to the motor from the boneyard on Monday.<BR>I'm from the Northwest,so the humidity here is just a little more than I'm used to.||||reg||1
Z||000026||terryk||07-14-2000||05:42 PM||||When I get this beast done, we can race to Eugene, OR. I'm near Sacramento.<P>I know you're up to your a$$ in alligators with finishing the swap so I appeciate you looking at the strut tower clearance.<P>I'll check into Chris's dogbone too.<P>Thanks again,<P>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
